WEBVTT

00:01.810 --> 00:05.720
Lady Rionne, what shall we do
about this sword?

00:05.720 --> 00:06.980
Call an appraiser.

00:07.450 --> 00:09.860
Determine its material composition at once.

00:09.860 --> 00:13.060
Find out who launched it
into the castle as well.

00:13.060 --> 00:13.750
Yes, milady!

00:16.780 --> 00:19.690
Whoever sent this sword flying here...

00:21.050 --> 00:23.310
must be powerful indeed.

01:58.060 --> 01:59.010
What's going on?

02:07.930 --> 02:10.580
Hey, what happened to them?

02:10.580 --> 02:13.600
They were attacked in 
the northern woods by a Skullface.

02:13.600 --> 02:14.260
What?

02:14.260 --> 02:19.390
Worse, of the twelve who 
went into the woods, only four survived.

02:19.390 --> 02:22.600
<i>So the attack must have been
the cause of the wreckage.</i>

02:22.600 --> 02:24.890
Also, it's not clear if it's related,

02:24.890 --> 02:29.400
but witnesses reported seeing a sword 
go flying out of the northern woods.

02:29.400 --> 02:32.540
Apparently, it crashed into the castle.

02:32.540 --> 02:33.420
What?

02:33.770 --> 02:36.010
Fortunately, nobody was hurt.

02:36.010 --> 02:37.220
Know anything about it?

02:37.220 --> 02:39.850
No. I was just out harvesting hilk grass.

02:39.850 --> 02:43.240
Well, if anything comes to you, let me know.

02:43.240 --> 02:45.090
The higher-ups have me on the case.

02:46.740 --> 02:49.170
Sorry. That was because of me.

02:51.560 --> 02:53.490
<i>I'm glad no one was hurt.</i>

02:53.490 --> 02:56.240
Welcome back, Shin.

02:56.240 --> 02:59.210
Celica! I stopped by to report in.

02:59.210 --> 03:01.570
Is all this commotion about the Skullface?

03:01.940 --> 03:05.040
Yes. Since it appeared near the kingdom,

03:05.040 --> 03:08.200
a high-priority extermination
request has been issued.

03:08.660 --> 03:11.570
Now then, what do you have to report?

03:12.820 --> 03:16.500
I thought I'd let you know that 
I defeated the Skullface Jack.

03:17.100 --> 03:18.960
Here's the gem I recovered.

03:19.610 --> 03:20.720
What?

03:21.100 --> 03:23.570
It was an odd one wielding a massive sword.

03:23.570 --> 03:25.470
Shattered my own blade to pieces.

03:25.470 --> 03:29.660
Wait a minute! Such a monster 
is not so easily slain!

03:29.660 --> 03:31.870
Hey, Celica, personal space!

03:31.870 --> 03:33.570
I-I'm so sorry!

03:35.300 --> 03:39.080
I mean, since you're normally so composed,
seeing you lose your cool

03:39.080 --> 03:40.240
is kinda, you know...

03:40.490 --> 03:41.440
What?

03:41.440 --> 03:45.530
Be that as it may, try not to tease
 my colleague too much.

03:45.530 --> 03:46.370
Els!

03:46.950 --> 03:48.170
Um...

03:48.170 --> 03:50.140
I'm Els. I work with Celica.

03:50.140 --> 03:52.200
She's told me all about you.

03:52.200 --> 03:53.620
Get this, Els!

03:54.310 --> 03:58.450
Shin claims he defeated the Skullface Jack.

03:58.450 --> 03:59.000
What?

03:59.470 --> 04:02.690
That said, I've got no way to prove it.

04:02.690 --> 04:06.640
The Skullface's gear was unimpressive, 
so I didn't bring it back with me.

04:06.640 --> 04:12.890
Getting your hands on Jack-level gear would
require either rank B or a small fortune.

04:12.890 --> 04:15.150
You scarcely sound like an adventurer.

04:15.590 --> 04:18.200
No matter. Let's examine that gem.

04:18.200 --> 04:21.280
It should contain the Skullface Jack's mana.

04:21.280 --> 04:24.530
Right. Shin, we'll be borrowing this.

04:24.530 --> 04:25.410
Sure.

04:25.910 --> 04:29.840
By the way, do Skullfaces frequently 
appear in the northern woods?

04:29.840 --> 04:34.920
Undead are born when mana fuses
with the lingering grudges of the fallen.

04:35.200 --> 04:37.500
The northern woods
are full of savage monsters,

04:37.500 --> 04:39.840
so no shortage of folks
have lost their lives there.

04:39.840 --> 04:44.430
I see. So the conditions 
are ripe for creating undead.

04:44.430 --> 04:47.700
But the mana of the woods itself isn't strong.

04:47.700 --> 04:50.430
We don't normally see Jack-level monsters.

04:50.810 --> 04:55.380
So this one was an exception. 
It was over level 300, even.

04:55.380 --> 04:57.560
Level 300? Really?

04:58.100 --> 05:00.240
Level 359, to be exact.

05:00.240 --> 05:01.820
It was probably unique.

05:01.820 --> 05:04.070
L-Level 359?

05:04.400 --> 05:09.060
Celica, gems can be used to determine
a monster's strength, right?

05:09.060 --> 05:11.600
Yes. I'll have this appraised right away.

05:11.600 --> 05:14.980
Els, I'm sorry, but could you 
man the reception desk?

05:15.490 --> 05:17.420
You can do that?

05:19.050 --> 05:21.060
You're rather nonchalant, aren't you?

05:21.060 --> 05:22.920
If you're right about its level,

05:22.920 --> 05:26.990
then you're at least as strong as
an A-rank party all by yourself.

05:28.210 --> 05:33.340
Erm, could you keep that between us? 
I don't want to attract attention.

05:33.940 --> 05:35.100
Understood.

05:35.480 --> 05:36.320
Excuse me!

05:36.320 --> 05:37.480
Welcome!

05:37.480 --> 05:38.980
Oh, Shin?

05:39.330 --> 05:42.290
Wait, huh? Cilica?

05:42.290 --> 05:44.490
Doesn't Celica work here, too?

05:44.800 --> 05:46.700
We're twins, after all.

05:46.700 --> 05:48.430
Now, right this way.

05:50.860 --> 05:54.680
Shin, do you mind sharing a table?

05:54.680 --> 05:58.410
Not at all. Sitting alone is awkward, anyway.

05:58.410 --> 05:59.500
Thanks so much.

06:16.420 --> 06:18.170
<i>The magic spear, "Venom."</i>

06:18.170 --> 06:23.250
<i>Said to be a legendary weapon, 
its abilities rival those of mythic arms.</i>

06:23.250 --> 06:25.580
Sorry to impose.

06:25.580 --> 06:28.610
Hey, I'm Shin. Nice to meet you.

06:29.170 --> 06:31.070
I'm Wilhelm Avis.

06:30.280 --> 06:33.530
<b>Wilhelm Avis</b>

06:30.280 --> 06:33.530
<b>Spearman</b>

06:31.070 --> 06:33.530
You a new adventurer?

06:33.530 --> 06:35.540
Oh, yeah. Today's my third day.

06:36.690 --> 06:39.040
Your equipment says otherwise.

06:39.340 --> 06:42.080
It's better than your average armor.

06:42.080 --> 06:43.820
I guess so.

06:44.250 --> 06:47.050
I'm from the sticks, so I don't know
what's normal around here.

06:47.590 --> 06:50.890
No wonder my name didn't scare you.

06:50.890 --> 06:53.050
Have you done something to frighten people?

06:54.490 --> 07:00.190
They call me Wilhelm the Vampire 
because I hunt so many undead.

07:00.190 --> 07:04.860
Seriously? So it's not because 
of that pale complexion?

07:04.860 --> 07:05.440
What?

07:05.440 --> 07:07.120
Is that guy stupid?

07:07.120 --> 07:09.630
I don't believe it! Does he have a death wish?

07:11.830 --> 07:15.450
You're a funny one.
This here is the real reason.

07:15.890 --> 07:18.610
Venom has the Drain ability.

07:18.610 --> 07:22.460
It consumes its victims' life force 
and transfers it to the wielder.

07:22.460 --> 07:26.340
I worry it might end up
 consuming <i>me</i> before I know it.

07:26.340 --> 07:28.340
So that's the story, huh?

07:28.340 --> 07:29.840
Sorry for the wait!

07:29.840 --> 07:31.280
This is for you, Shin.

07:31.280 --> 07:32.340
Ooh, it's here!

07:32.340 --> 07:34.640
And the usual for you, Wilhelm.

07:34.640 --> 07:35.350
Good.

07:36.020 --> 07:37.350
Take your time.

07:38.500 --> 07:39.850
Thanks.

07:39.850 --> 07:41.680
Well, shall we eat?

07:41.680 --> 07:42.820
Sounds good.

07:44.140 --> 07:46.740
I haven't been to a library in a while.

07:46.740 --> 07:49.740
I hope I can learn something about this world.

07:49.740 --> 07:53.740
<b>The Founding of Bayrelicht</b>

07:50.270 --> 07:53.740
Here we go. The annals of the
 Bayrelicht Kingdom.

07:55.430 --> 07:58.490
So it was founded 511 years ago...

07:58.940 --> 08:02.460
Tiera said the Dusk of Prosperity 
occurred 500 years ago.

08:02.460 --> 08:03.870
So that was around the same time.

08:04.410 --> 08:06.720
<i>You don't even know what that is?</i>

08:06.720 --> 08:10.190
<i>It was a major historical event 
when many people vanished.</i>

08:11.030 --> 08:16.340
Players disappear when they log out, 
so I can see why that caused confusion.

08:16.340 --> 08:19.180
I'd like to see more records, though.

08:19.850 --> 08:20.240
<b>Elf</b>

08:19.850 --> 08:21.270
<b>Dragnir</b>

08:19.850 --> 08:22.430
<b>Beast</b>

08:19.850 --> 08:25.730
<b>Dwarf</b>

08:20.300 --> 08:22.270
So these are the peoples of this world...

08:22.040 --> 08:25.730
<b>Pixie</b>

08:22.820 --> 08:25.190
They're basically the same
as in the in-game races.

08:23.410 --> 08:25.730
<b>Human</b>

08:23.710 --> 08:25.730
<b>Lord</b>

08:27.370 --> 08:29.950
Guess that's about all
I can gather from reading.

08:31.460 --> 08:33.930
Now then, let's begin this special council.

08:34.580 --> 08:38.530
The Skullface Jack that appeared 
in the northern woods has been slain.

08:38.530 --> 08:43.250
Its slayer returned only with its gem,
which is currently being examined.

08:43.700 --> 08:48.420
They defeated a Jack-level monster 
and didn't collect its sword or armor?

08:48.420 --> 08:51.450
The alleged slayer didn't find them
 particularly impressive.

08:51.450 --> 08:53.010
He wasn't <i>impressed</i>?

08:53.340 --> 08:57.900
There's always something strange 
about those with letters of introduction.

08:57.900 --> 08:59.640
Don't pay it too much mind.

08:59.640 --> 09:03.770
Wait, hold on now. <i>I'm</i> not that weird.

09:03.770 --> 09:06.420
That's hardly convincing coming from you.

09:06.420 --> 09:07.090
What?

09:08.730 --> 09:15.300
Anyway, the appraisal confirmed 
the gem to be level 359.

09:15.300 --> 09:16.240
So it's true.

09:16.740 --> 09:19.320
It's good to have confirmation,

09:19.320 --> 09:23.480
but the real question now is if
similar monsters are in the area.

09:23.480 --> 09:28.000
Though this one was a Skullface Jack, 
that level puts it on par with a King.

09:28.330 --> 09:32.010
I've already dispatched investigators 
to look into the matter.

09:32.010 --> 09:33.760
We'll have answers tomorrow.

09:33.760 --> 09:37.400
Skullfaces become active at night.

09:37.400 --> 09:41.060
I'd like the knights to be on their guard.

09:41.060 --> 09:44.500
Understood, but I have a question.

09:44.500 --> 09:45.270
What is it?

09:45.710 --> 09:51.660
I heard the Skullface 
brandished unusual equipment.

09:51.660 --> 09:56.030
I'd like to know more about that 
and the person who defeated it.

09:56.550 --> 09:58.800
I can tell you about the weapon,

09:58.800 --> 10:02.030
but the slayer has asked 
to keep their identity a secret.

10:02.620 --> 10:03.860
Why do you want to know?

10:04.260 --> 10:06.330
The day that sword flew into the castle

10:06.650 --> 10:10.820
was the day this Skullface
with remarkable gear was taken down.

10:11.490 --> 10:14.300
Some believe the two are related.

10:15.610 --> 10:17.670
What kind of sword is it?

10:18.380 --> 10:20.350
Please keep this between us.

10:20.890 --> 10:22.700
The blade's roughly two mels long,

10:22.700 --> 10:25.620
made of an alloy of magic steel and mithril.

10:25.620 --> 10:28.980
It's even permanently enchanted
 with the light element.

10:28.980 --> 10:30.530
In other words...

10:30.530 --> 10:33.580
Yes. It's comparable to, if not greater than,

10:33.580 --> 10:35.690
our nation's royal sword.

10:35.690 --> 10:39.700
What? But that would make it legendary.

10:39.960 --> 10:42.900
So you can't blame me
for being curious about who

10:42.900 --> 10:45.360
defeated a monster wielding such a blade.

10:45.360 --> 10:48.460
Moreover, there's something of a problem...

10:50.530 --> 10:51.750
What's that?

10:53.060 --> 10:56.210
Man, gathering information sure is difficult.

10:56.520 --> 10:58.770
What should I do now?

11:01.220 --> 11:02.720
<i>Stare...</i>

11:05.130 --> 11:06.810
<i>Stare...</i>

11:08.370 --> 11:11.600
Uh, you want some?

11:21.320 --> 11:23.330
<i>Is she a tiger-type beast girl?</i>

11:23.330 --> 11:25.740
<i>She doesn't look like a beggar.</i>

11:26.230 --> 11:27.390
<i>Is she lost?</i>

11:27.850 --> 11:29.700
Thanks for the meal.

11:29.700 --> 11:30.870
You're very welcome.

11:31.410 --> 11:34.130
I'm Millie. You're a nice guy.

11:34.570 --> 11:36.980
Thanks. I'm Shin.

11:36.980 --> 11:38.220
Shin!

11:38.220 --> 11:40.290
I'm going home now. What about you?

11:40.290 --> 11:41.270
Should I walk you?

11:41.870 --> 11:43.390
He's here to pick me up!

11:44.290 --> 11:46.890
Hey, I wasn't expecting to run into you again.

11:47.730 --> 11:49.660
Right back at you.

11:49.660 --> 11:50.640
Wil!

11:51.950 --> 11:53.400
Is she your kid?

11:53.760 --> 11:57.810
No way. She's one of the kids 
from the church orphanage.

11:57.810 --> 12:00.140
Millie's good at sneaking out,

12:00.140 --> 12:02.780
so I always come to find her.

12:02.780 --> 12:03.780
I see.

12:04.220 --> 12:07.720
Anyway, I'm surprised she's 
taken a liking to you.

12:07.720 --> 12:09.540
She's actually pretty shy.

12:09.930 --> 12:11.330
Is that right?

12:11.330 --> 12:13.580
Now, let's go home, Millie.

12:13.580 --> 12:14.820
Wait a second.

12:19.780 --> 12:21.170
...in the northern woods.

12:21.170 --> 12:22.920
Please save them.

12:23.770 --> 12:24.370
What?

12:27.990 --> 12:29.300
Bye-bye!

12:37.180 --> 12:39.230
<i>Why did Millie ask me to do that?</i>

12:40.030 --> 12:42.290
<i>There's a fox in the northern woods.</i>

12:42.290 --> 12:43.820
<i>Please save them.</i>

12:44.460 --> 12:50.210
<i>They must be in danger if she 
wants me to save them, but why me?</i>

12:51.260 --> 12:55.010
Guess I've got nothing better to do 
until Schnee returns.

12:55.010 --> 12:56.580
I'll check out the northern woods.

12:56.890 --> 13:00.020
Wait, I know a way 
to get in touch with her.

13:00.540 --> 13:01.730
I'll give it a shot.

13:02.090 --> 13:04.090
<b>Moon Sanctum</b>

13:04.670 --> 13:06.120
Welcome!

13:06.120 --> 13:07.340
Oh, Shin!

13:07.340 --> 13:10.740
Hey. I forgot to leave a message the other day.

13:10.740 --> 13:12.850
Oh, right. You mentioned that.

13:12.850 --> 13:17.980
Anyway, could you tell her, "If you recognize
 this, I'd like to meet and catch up"?

13:20.010 --> 13:22.250
Is this an ancient weapon?

13:22.250 --> 13:23.610
Huh? You can tell?

13:24.340 --> 13:26.810
This is Schnee's sword, Blue Moon.

13:26.810 --> 13:28.340
It belongs to my master?

13:28.340 --> 13:28.990
Yeah.

13:29.510 --> 13:34.000
It can only be used by its creators, 
me and Schnee, or people we designate.

13:34.000 --> 13:36.280
So its wielders are limited?

13:36.280 --> 13:37.500
That's right.

13:38.010 --> 13:43.020
Huh. I can tell that it's a powerful weapon.

13:43.670 --> 13:45.920
But I wouldn't want to use it.

13:45.920 --> 13:46.760
Why not?

13:47.310 --> 13:51.260
I feel like it'd swallow me up.

13:51.910 --> 13:55.770
Maybe that's coming from the base materials.

13:56.190 --> 13:58.720
It's primarily made of a chimeradite alloy,

13:58.720 --> 14:05.070
plus a Black Death Dragon fang, 
Ocean Thrasher scale, and Elementail tear.

14:05.070 --> 14:06.170
And then...

14:06.170 --> 14:08.030
Wait, what's wrong, Tiera?

14:08.030 --> 14:10.780
I'm okay. I'm fine.

14:11.140 --> 14:17.090
Rattle off all the legendary monsters you 
want. I won't be surprised anymore.

14:17.090 --> 14:19.420
Y-You don't look okay at all.

14:20.780 --> 14:24.920
Everything stops making sense 
when you're around.

14:24.920 --> 14:26.510
Sorry, I guess.

14:26.970 --> 14:30.800
But Blue Moon will tell me
if Schnee remembers me or not.

14:30.800 --> 14:32.970
Fine. I'll hold on to it.

14:32.970 --> 14:36.590
Also, use these to let me know 
if you hear from Schnee.

14:37.150 --> 14:40.690
They're one-way, but they'll reach me 
no matter where I am.

14:41.170 --> 14:45.220
Just write the recipient's name and say "send."

14:45.220 --> 14:47.370
What a convenient item.

14:47.770 --> 14:50.850
But couldn't you send her a message yourself?

14:50.850 --> 14:53.700
I wondered that myself
and tried last night, but...

14:54.290 --> 14:57.290
<i>Send! Send! Send!</i>

14:55.700 --> 14:57.290
It didn't work.

14:57.290 --> 14:59.890
Do these actually work, then?

15:00.430 --> 15:01.730
Good question.

15:01.730 --> 15:03.030
Hold on.

15:10.700 --> 15:13.200
I got it, Shin!

15:13.200 --> 15:16.060
Huh. There's nothing wrong 
with the cards, then,

15:16.060 --> 15:18.930
but for some reason, 
I can't send them to Schnee.

15:19.670 --> 15:24.840
<i>It's probably dependent on whether
or not you've met someone in this world.</i>

15:24.840 --> 15:30.260
Say, Shin, could I get a few of these letters?

15:30.260 --> 15:33.440
Sure. I've got more than I need.

15:33.440 --> 15:37.120
Thank you! I'm actually trying
to become a mage,

15:37.120 --> 15:40.180
so I'd like to study this magic item.

15:40.180 --> 15:43.940
Okay. That should cover the cost 
of leaving a message, right?

15:43.940 --> 15:44.830
Of course!

15:45.590 --> 15:48.650
Well, I should get going. 
Say hi to Schnee for me.

15:48.650 --> 15:50.150
You can count on me.

15:50.720 --> 15:53.720
<b>Moon Sanctum</b>

15:52.950 --> 15:55.790
Now, what should I try first?

15:56.810 --> 16:00.230
Wait, shouldn't I send 
one of these to my master?

16:02.300 --> 16:04.230
I'm here in the northern woods,

16:04.230 --> 16:08.340
but I have no idea how to go about
saving this fox.

16:08.340 --> 16:10.990
For now, I'll try heading deeper.

16:12.020 --> 16:17.740
Leave... Leave... Leave...

16:17.740 --> 16:19.610
<i>Is this a barrier?</i>

16:19.610 --> 16:23.370
<i>I've enhanced my resistance to mental 
interference, so it has no effect on me,</i>

16:23.890 --> 16:27.190
<i>but it's a strong sign that there's 
something up ahead.</i>

16:27.750 --> 16:36.260
Leave... Leave... Leave... Leave...

16:42.030 --> 16:43.270
A shrine?

16:44.350 --> 16:46.540
The mental interference is gone.

16:46.540 --> 16:48.700
So this is the heart of the barrier.

16:54.490 --> 16:57.630
What was that?
I just heard something shatter.

17:09.050 --> 17:11.250
I don't see any traps.

17:16.330 --> 17:18.730
This must be the one Millie was talking about.

17:18.970 --> 17:21.560
<b>Poison X</b>

17:18.970 --> 17:21.560
<b>Curse X</b>

17:18.970 --> 17:21.560
<b>Analyze</b>

17:19.830 --> 17:23.560
What? It's poisoned <i>and</i> cursed? It's dying!

17:23.900 --> 17:25.210
I'd better cure it.

17:35.930 --> 17:37.070
What was that sound?

17:38.230 --> 17:40.580
Must've been the barrier breaking.

17:45.070 --> 17:46.960
That's a lot of enemies.

17:47.630 --> 17:49.960
Sorry, but hang tight for a minute.

17:50.420 --> 17:52.580
I'm gonna clear these guys out of the way.

17:53.530 --> 17:55.610
After the incident with the unique monster,

17:55.610 --> 17:57.470
I don't want any more casualties.

17:58.140 --> 17:59.720
Sorry, but...

18:01.620 --> 18:03.220
none of you are getting away!

18:06.560 --> 18:07.560
Furrow Pierce!

18:09.520 --> 18:11.310
Next, Flashing Blossom!

18:16.230 --> 18:17.660
Done and dusted.

18:18.310 --> 18:20.730
What should I do now?

18:22.650 --> 18:24.370
They weren't here before.

18:32.710 --> 18:33.460
What?

18:46.720 --> 18:49.730
Seriously? I've never seen these before.

18:49.850 --> 18:54.230
<b>Monster</b>

18:49.850 --> 18:54.230
<b>Invaded Golem</b>

18:50.790 --> 18:54.230
Invaded Golem, level 674?

18:54.520 --> 18:57.240
I see. So that black haze is a miasma.

18:59.850 --> 19:00.990
Whoa!

19:04.740 --> 19:07.500
The miasma's making them behave erratically.

19:08.740 --> 19:12.180
I have no quarrel with them, 
but I can't just leave them at large.

19:12.180 --> 19:14.030
Hold on a little longer.

19:16.210 --> 19:17.630
Shadow Bind!

19:29.250 --> 19:32.130
A smokescreen? It can't be ordinary mist.

19:33.730 --> 19:36.420
Not good... The miasma is hurting it.

19:36.420 --> 19:37.870
I'd better finish this quickly.

19:39.940 --> 19:41.700
My Shadow Bind wore off!

19:43.770 --> 19:46.830
<i>I can't pinpoint the enemy's
location in this darkness.</i>

19:49.710 --> 19:52.530
<i>If I use my full strength,
I'll hurt this little one, too.</i>

19:52.530 --> 19:54.050
<i>But at this rate...</i>

19:55.670 --> 19:56.750
What is it?

19:59.500 --> 20:01.010
There's something over there?

20:01.860 --> 20:03.710
The magic circle you were in.

20:06.090 --> 20:08.270
The mist hasn't breached it.

20:09.020 --> 20:11.520
I can see into the mist from here.

20:12.410 --> 20:14.890
Thanks. We'll be fine now.

20:18.140 --> 20:19.650
The enemy's caught on, too.

20:19.650 --> 20:21.150
But it's too late.

20:22.130 --> 20:23.280
Arc Bind!

20:27.300 --> 20:28.910
This ends now!

20:28.910 --> 20:29.790
Cataclysmic Strike!

20:39.190 --> 20:40.670
What a mess.

20:40.960 --> 20:43.890
But the miasma is gone now.

20:43.890 --> 20:45.180
That just leaves...

20:46.830 --> 20:50.650
Whoa, there. Looks like you're all better now.

20:51.550 --> 20:54.270
Come to think of it, 
you're a Little Fox, right?

20:54.740 --> 20:56.490
Let's check and see.

20:56.100 --> 20:58.270
<b>Monster</b>

20:56.100 --> 20:58.270
<b>Elementail</b>

20:57.580 --> 20:58.270
What?

20:58.270 --> 20:59.770
An Elementail?!

20:58.270 --> 20:59.770
<b>Monster</b>

20:58.270 --> 20:59.770
<b>Elementail</b>

21:00.490 --> 21:04.920
Even in <i>THE NEW GATE</i>, 
they were top-tier monsters.

21:04.920 --> 21:08.280
But you should look humanoid 
or like a giant fox.

21:08.280 --> 21:10.900
I've never heard of a kit version before.

21:12.620 --> 21:14.780
Well, no point in thinking about it.

21:14.780 --> 21:16.670
What are you going to do now?

21:17.670 --> 21:19.180
You wanna come with me?

21:21.870 --> 21:24.860
Ow, ow, ow! Calm down.

21:26.010 --> 21:29.350
You definitely understand me, don't you?

21:30.750 --> 21:35.060
<i>Golems afflicted with miasma 
and an Elementail kit...</i>

21:35.660 --> 21:38.570
<i>Those never appeared in the game,</i>

21:38.570 --> 21:41.750
<i>but they could be a hint 
about how to get back to my world.</i>

21:42.500 --> 21:45.410
I should ask Millie about this little one.

21:46.590 --> 21:48.570
I told you, that hurts!

21:52.610 --> 21:54.490
A letter for me?

21:54.890 --> 21:57.330
What's Tiera doing with this magic item?

22:02.670 --> 22:03.780
Master!

23:35.050 --> 23:40.060
<b>Next Time
Episode 3
<b>A Strange Request</b></b>
